From edf0af51c5cd53b3c3c611e21ec57b0852f34b73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Klein <d.klein@gsi.de>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:12:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(algorithm): FastFFT for complex power-of-two sizes

`gr::algorithm::FFT` routes complex, power-of-two transforms with N >= 64 to `FastFFT` when std::simd is native (libstdc++ via vir-simd), and keeps SimdFFT for everything else (real transforms, other sizes, and Clang and Emscripten builds, where vir-simd falls back to arrays).

```cpp
gr::algorithm::FFT<std::complex<float>> fft;          // FastFFT by default
fft.compute(signal, spectrum);
fft.useFastFFT = false;                                // back to SimdFFT

gr::algorithm::FastFFT<float> plan;                    // or directly
plan.resize(4096UZ);
plan.forward(signal, spectrum);                        // in == out allowed
```

`FastFFT` is a Stockham autosort FFT on `vir::stdx::native_simd`: a radix-8 first pass vectorised over butterflies and transposed in registers, radix-16 middle passes with broadcast twiddles, one twiddle-free radix-2/4/8/16 final pass.
The only non-std::simd construct is `__builtin_shufflevector` (GCC and Clang) for the two-input shuffles that std::simd lacks; no ISA intrinsics.
Design, method and cross-host measurements (including FFTW): https://github.com/dennisklein/fft

`bm_FFT_backends`, complex float, single transform, median, GCC trunk `-O2 -march=native`, one pinned core of a Xeon VM with AVX-512:

| N      | SimdFFT | FastFFT | SyclFFT:CPU |
| -----: | ------: | ------: | ----------: |
| 1024   | 3 us    | 2 us    | 2 us        |
| 4096   | 18 us   | 10 us   | 12 us       |
| 16384  | 81 us   | 38 us   | 56 us       |
| 65536  | 390 us  | 204 us  | 313 us      |

### Changes

- `FastFFT.hpp`: `FastFFT<T>` (float, double) and its SIMD kernel
- `fft.hpp`: dispatch to `FastFFT` behind `useFastFFT` (default on), compiled out where std::simd is emulated
- `qa_FastFFT`: against a direct DFT for N = 64..4096, impulse and tone with analytic spectra up to N = 2^18, in place vs out of place, `FFT` with `useFastFFT` on vs off
- `bm_FFT_backends`: a FastFFT row next to SimdFFT
